   (at your option) any later version.

   Symbols libWebKit exports. Without this it exports everything it links
   (about 217,000 symbols: WebCore, JSC, OpenSSL, ICU...), and the SDK's
   rtld (crt/rtld_so.c) looks each symbol up with a linear strcmp over the
   whole table: loading libWebKit took longer than 90 s and the app never
   reached main(). Hidden symbols are bound when libWebKit is linked, so
   their relocations need no lookup at all.

   Exported: the C API apps use (WK*, JS*), the entry points of the child
   processes and the process-launcher API they share with libWebKit. */
{
  global:
    WK*;
    JS*;
    kJS*;
    extern "C++" {
      "WebKit::WebProcessMain(int, char**)";
      "WebKit::NetworkProcessMain(int, char**)";
      PlayStation::*;
    };
    __syscall;
  local:
    *;
};
